        "question": {
          ":question/id": "f035726e-08b8-5684-beec-6c89d1b492b7",
          ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
          ":question/problem": "![](/tmp/ca9837-templates-703c6brn/17592186096814/344964b4a4941e009c5a619505322bdcfa6872c1c7219d36cc40c06e9d637508-prompt.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $a$. Choose the unit vector in the same direction.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "![](/tmp/ca9837-templates-703c6brn/17592186096814/344964b4a4941e009c5a619505322bdcfa6872c1c7219d36cc40c06e9d637508-solution.png)\n\nIn $\\bigtriangleup AHB$ we have $\\angle AHB=90^\\circ$, $AH=3$ and $BH=5$. So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB &= \\sqrt{AH^2+BH^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(3)^2+(5)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{9+25} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{34}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the magnitude of $a$ is $\\sqrt{34}$. Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{1}{|a|}\\cdot a \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{34}}{34}a\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
